    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ten thousand years ago, the first people came to the high plains of Wright to hunt buffalo and antelope.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ranchers arrived in the 1880s to graze longhorn cattle and sheep on the open range around Wright.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Wright family homesteaded the area in 1911, creating the community and opening the town's first post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wright boomed in the 1970s with the creation of the Black Thunder Coal Mine, the most productive mine in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
